    "lawCode": "Amd §4-104, EL L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5029\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to the use of certain\nbuildings as polling places accessible to persons with disabilities\n\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThe bill requires that people and entities that control buildings,\nwhich receive tax breaks, subsidies or get construction grants or\nloans, make rooms available in the building for registration and\nvoting if the board finds the rooms suitable for that purpose and\naccessible to the disabled without restriction as to the size of the\nmunicipality where the building is located.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1: Amends Election Law subdivisions 3-a and 3-b of 4-104 to\nremove the limitation to cities with populations of over one hundred\nthousand from the requirement that if a building receives public\nbenefits they must make rooms available for voter registration and\nvoting.\n\nSection 2: Provides for the Act to take effect on the first day of\nDecember after it becomes a law.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nUnder current law, rooms were only required to be made available in\nsuch buildings in they were located in a city with a population of\nover one hundred thousand.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nAs a result of federal and state statutes, the legislature has\nestablished a goal of full polling place accessibility. The 1989 law\npartially achieved this goal in the State's larger cities where\npolling places of any kind were not readily available, but exempted\nbuildings in smaller cities.  However, since 1989, it has become\napparent that there is the same pressing need in the suburbs.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2008; A.3058- Assembly Election Law 2007; A.3058- Assembly Election\nLaw 2005-06; A.5845- Assembly Election Law 2003-04; A.4776- Assembly\nElection Law 2001-02; A.4563- Assembly Election Law 1999-00; A.4760-\nAssembly Election Law 1997-98; A.3890- Assembly Election Law 1995-96;\nA.6111- Passed Assembly 1993-94; A.5179Passed Assembly 1991-92;\nA.3868- Passed Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act takes effect on December One after the date it becomes a law.\n",
